/// ParticleWall OnPlay gains block only. Bead `sts2-rs-4nhp1`: the
/// return-to-hand was moved OUT of the handler into the play-finish disposal
/// step (`combat_loop::finish_card_play`, C# `GetResultPileTypeForCardPlay`:
/// Discard -> Hand) so the resolving card stays on the Play pile across replays
/// — an inline move emptied the Play pile mid-resolve and crashed
/// `current_block`'s `play.last()` on the next replay ("dispatch: empty Play
/// pile"). The return-to-hand routing is now covered by
/// `sts2-core combat_loop::tests::particle_wall_defers_return_to_hand_to_disposal`;
/// this test (which dispatches the handler in isolation, without the disposal
/// step) asserts only the block leg. Bead `sts2-rs-653b` originally retrofitted
/// this from a block-only baseline.
#[test]
